They indicate stress. The rationale is that spaces shouldn't matter in
text, because in speech they don't exist. selpa'i also assigns a breve on
the i and u when used as approximants in e.g. {ua} and {ia}, because they
represent different sounds than simple {i} and {u}. Finally, selpa'i uses
an under-dot on the second letter of a diphthong, so the {i} in {coi} would
have one.

.i mi'e la tsani mu'o

